course: dictionary
lesson: 14000
title: The word lowest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lowest is a special form of the word low, which means not high. When we compare three or more things, we add -est to get lowest. It can mean the least high, the smallest amount, or the deepest sound. «The lowest shelf is the one nearest the floor.» Here lowest tells you which shelf is at the bottom.
explain: Lowest often means the smallest number or amount among several things. «Our class had the lowest score in the test.» That means no other score was smaller. When you see "the" and a group of things being compared, lowest usually means the smallest.
explain: Lowest can also describe sound. «The lowest note on the piano is on the far left.» A low note is deep, so the lowest note is the deepest one of all. To check your meaning, put another word in its place, such as smallest or deepest, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Lowest is the superlative form of low: low, lower, lowest.
fact: «Lowest» means the least high, nearest the ground or the bottom.
fact: «Lowest» can mean the smallest number or amount, such as the lowest price.
fact: «Lowest» can mean the quietest or deepest sound, such as the lowest note.
fact: Use lowest when you compare three or more things.
exercise: «The lowest shelf is the one nearest the floor.» What does lowest mean here? | The longest, going along the wall | The highest, nearest the ceiling | The brightest, with the most light | *The least high, nearest the bottom
exercise: «Our class had the lowest score in the test.» What does lowest mean here? | The best and highest score | The most popular score | The score that was read out first | *The smallest number of points
exercise: Which word completes the list: low, lower, ___? | *lowest | loudest | lowering | high
test: «The lowest price in the shop was for a pencil.» What does lowest mean? | The most expensive | *The smallest amount of money | The longest | The heaviest
test: Which word means the deepest note in music? | Fastest | Loudest | *Lowest | Highest
exam: Maya says lowest always means the bottom of something. Is she right? | Yes, and it also means the highest point | No, lowest only means the loudest sound | Yes, lowest only ever means the floor | *No, lowest can also mean the smallest amount or the deepest sound
